    honorificAr: "عليه السلام",
    summary: "Idris followed the religion of Adam and Seth after people began to drift from tawhid. Ibn Kathir relates that he called the people of Babylon to return to truth: justice between people, prayer,…",
    content: "Birth and Teachings\n\nIdris followed the religion of Adam and Seth after people began to drift from tawhid. Ibn Kathir relates that he called the people of Babylon to return to truth: justice between people, prayer, fasting on certain days, and giving a portion of wealth to the poor. Only a few listened, so he and those who believed moved on, continuing to teach fairness wherever they settled.\n\nRaised in Station\n\nThe Quran names him among the truthful and the prophets, and states that Allah raised him to a high station. Commentators preserved wise sayings attributed to him about patience, honesty, and remembering death. Though brief, his chapter in Stories of the Prophets places him as an early link in the chain of guidance whenever communities forget Allah.",
    contentAr: "سار إدريس على دين آدم وشيث، فدعا أهل بابل إلى الحق والعدل والصلاة والصيام والصدقة، فلم يستجب إلا قليل. فخرج بمن معه يعلّم القسط. وأثنى عليه القرآن بأنه صدّيق نبي رفعه الله مكاناً عليّاً. وعدّه ابن كثير في أوائل الهداة بعد آدم، تذكيراً بأن النبوة تتواصل كلما انحرف الناس.",
